From: relay12 contributors
Subject: [PATCH] dtl: make the write-state bitmask a portable const

llvm-mingw's winnt.h does not mark the operators DEFINE_ENUM_FLAG_OPERATORS
generates as constexpr, unlike the MSVC SDK headers this project was
originally written against. RESOURCE_STATE_ALL_WRITE_BITS combines several
D3D12_RESOURCE_STATES enumerators through that non-constexpr operator| while
itself declared constexpr, so Clang rejects the initializer as not a
constant expression; MSVC's constexpr operator| let this compile unnoticed.

const carries the same implicit internal linkage a namespace-scope
constexpr variable already had and needs no compile-time-constant
initializer, only an ordinary one, which is unaffected by whether the
operator computing it happens to be constexpr. The only other reference to
this variable is a plain runtime bitwise-AND comparison, so nothing here
depended on it being a core constant expression.
---
diff --git a/include/ResourceState.hpp b/include/ResourceState.hpp
index 11c2d20..8adf16f 100644
--- a/include/ResourceState.hpp
+++ b/include/ResourceState.hpp
@@ -10,7 +10,7 @@ namespace D3D12TranslationLayer
 #define UNKNOWN_RESOURCE_STATE (D3D12_RESOURCE_STATES)0x8000u
 #define RESOURCE_STATE_VALID_BITS 0x2f3fff
 #define RESOURCE_STATE_VALID_INTERNAL_BITS 0x2fffff
-constexpr D3D12_RESOURCE_STATES RESOURCE_STATE_ALL_WRITE_BITS =
+const D3D12_RESOURCE_STATES RESOURCE_STATE_ALL_WRITE_BITS =
     D3D12_RESOURCE_STATE_RENDER_TARGET          |
     D3D12_RESOURCE_STATE_UNORDERED_ACCESS       |
     D3D12_RESOURCE_STATE_DEPTH_WRITE            |
